WEBVTT

00:10:27.289 --> 00:10:31.293
I'm talking about the 2009 outbreak
of the H1N1 flu.

00:10:32.044 --> 00:10:35.005
And we have to stop repeating
the same mistakes.

00:10:35.547 --> 00:10:37.341
So let's be imaginative

00:10:37.341 --> 00:10:41.095
about how we challenge
businesses and government

00:10:41.136 --> 00:10:44.556
to use shared risk,

00:10:44.598 --> 00:10:48.811
supply-chain transparency
and automated recommendations

00:10:48.852 --> 00:10:51.271
to make our supply chains more resilient.

00:10:51.313 --> 00:10:52.731
Because if they do,

00:10:52.773 --> 00:10:54.692
we can be more resilient too.

00:10:55.359 --> 00:10:56.527
Thank you.

00:10:56.568 --> 00:10:58.362
(Cheers and applause)